{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Neither, etc.</b> Even a plant that has a head and a tail — it shall not be his. And some say it is a metaphor, for he is astray and does not know what to do, and behold he will not perform the deed of the <b>head</b>, who is an elder and a man of standing (Isaiah 9:14); the <b>tail</b> is the rest of the multitude. And likewise כפה ואגמון [a reed and rush]:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The phrase ולא וגו׳ ('Neither, etc.') abbreviates the verse's ולא־יהיה להם מעשה; rendered as the lemma head."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:19.520375805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}